{"case_id":"C109","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":97,"change_types":["internal numeric-conversion implementation change","buffer-size adjustment"],"affected_functions":["json_loadb","json_dumps","json_dump_callback","jsonp_strtod","jsonp_dtostr","dtoa_r"],"reason":"The commit replaces the internal floating-point formatting path with dtoa-based logic, but it does not introduce a new public entry point, protocol, initialization requirement, or input constraint. The existing harness already sends arbitrary bytes through json_loadb, which can create real values, and then serializes successful values through both json_dumps and json_dump_callback with fuzz-controlled dump flags, including JSON_REAL_PRECISION. Those high-level paths invoke the changed jsonp_dtostr/dtoa_r implementation, so no harness maintenance is required.","evidence":["The harness calls json_loadb(text, size, load_flags, &error) on the fuzz-controlled payload.","After a successful load, the harness calls either json_dumps(jobj, dump_flags & ~JSON_MAX_INDENT) or json_dump_callback(jobj, json_dump_counter, &counter, dump_flags).","dump_flags are derived directly from fuzz input and include the JSON_REAL_PRECISION field shown by ((dump_flags >> 11) & 0x1F) << 11.","src/strconv.c changes jsonp_dtostr internally to call dtoa_r when DTOA_ENABLED; no new caller-facing arguments or setup are added.","src/dump.c only reduces MAX_INTEGER_STR_LENGTH and MAX_REAL_STR_LENGTH from 100 to 25."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing harness unchanged; it already exercises the modified real-number parsing and serialization paths with fuzz-controlled JSON data and formatting flags."}
